metric cosets using inverse DFT. The cosets are `init * g^i * D` for `i = 0,...,width-1` where `D` is a smooth subgroup.\n\n**Process:**\n1. Performs IDFT within each coset to get remainders modulo `X^height - shift^height`\n2. Unshifts coefficients by `(init * shift^i)^{-t}`\n3. Interpolates across cosets using Lagrange basis for geometric points\n4. Returns univariate polynomial in coefficient form\n\n---\n\n### 7. **DeviceBuffer Type and Key Methods**\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/src/d_buffer.rs`\n\n```rust\n#[repr(C)]\npub struct DeviceBuffer<T> {\n    ptr: *mut T,\n    len: usize,\n}\n\nimpl<T> DeviceBuffer<T> {\n    pub fn new() -> Self  // Creates empty buffer (null pointer, zero length)\n    pub fn with_capacity(len: usize) -> Self  // Allocates device memory for `len` elements\n    pub fn as_ptr(&self) -> *const T  // Returns const typed pointer\n    pub fn as_mut_ptr(&self) -> *mut T  // Returns mutable typed pointer\n    pub fn as_raw_ptr(&self) -> *const c_void  // Returns untyped const pointer\n    pub fn as_mut_raw_ptr(&self) -> *mut c_void  // Returns untyped mutable pointer\n    pub fn len(&self) -> usize  // Returns number of elements\n    pub fn is_empty(&self) -> bool  // Checks if null or zero length\n    pub fn fill_zero(&self) -> Result<(), CudaError>  // Fills buffer with zeros (async)\n    pub fn fill_zero_suffix(&self, start_idx: usize) -> Result<(), CudaError>  // Zeros suffix\n    pub fn as_buffer<U>(mut self) -> DeviceBuffer<U>  // Type-casts buffer\n    pub fn view(&self) -> DeviceBufferView  // Creates non-owning view\n}\n```\n\n**Memory copy traits (from cuda-common/src/copy.rs):**\n\n```rust\n// Device -> Host\npub trait MemCopyD2H<T> {\n    fn to_host(&self) -> Result<Vec<T>, MemCopyError>;\n}\n\n// Device -> Host (stream-synchronized version, safe for multi-threaded access)\npub trait MemCopyD2HStreamSync<T> {\n    fn to_host_on_current_stream(&self) -> Result<Vec<T>, MemCopyError>;\n}\n\n// Host -> Device\npub trait MemCopyH2D<T> {\n    fn copy_to(&self, dst: &mut DeviceBuffer<T>) -> Result<(), MemCopyError>;\n    fn to_device(&self) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<T>, MemCopyError>;\n}\n```\n\n**Implementation for DeviceBuffer:**\n- `to_host()`: Copies to host via `cudaMemcpyAsync` on `cudaStreamPerThread`, then synchronizes via global COPY_EVENT mutex\n- `to_host_on_current_stream()`: Copies to host and synchronizes on the calling thread's per-thread stream (safe for multi-threaded use)\n\n---\n\n### 8. **Frac Type Definition**\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/stark-backend/src/prover/logup_zerocheck/fractional_sumcheck_gkr.rs` (lines 29-45)\n\n```rust\n#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Default, derive_new::new)]\n#[repr(C)]\npub struct Frac<EF> {\n    // PERF[jpw]: in the initial round, we can keep `p` in base field\n    pub p: EF,\n    pub q: EF,\n}\n\nimpl<EF: Field> Add<Frac<EF>> for Frac<EF> {\n    type Output = Frac<EF>;\n\n    fn add(self, other: Frac<EF>) -> Self::Output {\n        Frac {\n            p: self.p * other.q + self.q * other.p,\n            q: self.q * other.q,\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**Purpose:** Represents fractions in projective coordinates: `p/q`. Used for fractional sumcheck protocol. The `#[repr(C)]` makes it safe to pass to CUDA kernels.\n\n**Type aliases:**\n- `EF` is defined in `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/types.rs` as `BabyBearPoseidon2Config::EF`\n- The struct is generic to support both base field and extension field numerators\n\n---\n\n### 9. **Round0ThreadBuffers Struct**\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs` (lines 28-33)\n\n```rust\npub(crate) struct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n    pub zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    pub zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    pub logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    pub logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,\n}\n```\n\n**Purpose:** Pre-allocated per-thread GPU buffers for Round 0 evaluation. Reused across AIRs to eliminate per-AIR mutex contention on the global memory manager.\n\n**Usage pattern** (lines 1088-1127):\n- Created as `Vec<Round0ThreadBuffers>` with one entry per thread\n- Each field is either allocated with `DeviceBuffer::with_capacity()` or created empty with `DeviceBuffer::new()`\n- Buffers are conditionally pre-allocated based on available memory budget\n- Reused and passed to both `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` and `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()`\n\n**Key functions that use Round0ThreadBuffers:**\n\n**evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu** (lines 40-154):\n```rust\npub fn evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    eq_cube: *const EF,\n    lambda_pows: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    skip_domain: u32,\n    num_x: u32,\n    height: u32,\n    num_cosets: u32,\n    g_shift: F,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n    prealloc_intermediates: Option<&mut DeviceBuffer<F>>,\n    prealloc_temp_sums: Option<&mut DeviceBuffer<EF>>,\n) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<EF>, Round0EvalError>\n```\n\n**evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu** (lines 162-220, see file):\n```rust\npub fn evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu<HS: GpuHashScheme>(\n    pk: &DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    symbolic: &SymbolicConstraints<F>,\n    selectors_cube: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    main_parts: &DeviceBuffer<*const F>,\n    public_values: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    eq_cube: *const EF,\n    beta_pows: &[EF],\n    eq_3bs: &[EF],\n    skip_domain: u32,\n    num_x: u32,\n    height: u32,\n    num_cosets: u32,\n    g_shift: F,\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n    prealloc_intermediates: Option<&mut DeviceBuffer<F>>,\n    // ...\n) -> Result<DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>, LogupZerocheckError>\n```\n\n---\n\n### 10. **Type Aliases and Field Definitions**\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/types.rs`\n\n```rust\npu