{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016M7eRkYKqcYkCBrzjWVo7j","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me compile the comprehensive report:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've thoroughly analyzed the CUDA-side type definitions and patterns in this stark-backend project. Here are my detailed findings:\n\n### 1. FpExt Type Definition\n\n**File**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-common/include/fpext.h`\n\n**Type Definition (lines 38-122)**:\n```cuda\nstruct FpExt {\n    /// The elements of FpExt, elems[0] + elems[1]*X + elems[2]*X^2 + elems[3]*x^4\n    union {\n        Fp elems[4];\n        bb31_4_t rep;\n    };\n    // ... constructors and operators\n};\n```\n\n**Key Facts**:\n- `FpExt` represents elements of a finite field F_p^4\n- Based on the irreducible polynomial x^4 - 11\n- Represents elements as: `elems[0] + elems[1]*X + elems[2]*X^2 + elems[3]*X^3`\n- You access fields using: `.elems[0]`, `.elems[1]`, `.elems[2]`, `.elems[3]` (NOT `.c0`, `.c1`, etc.)\n- Can also use `.rep` for the underlying `bb31_4_t` representation\n- Size: 16 bytes (4 * 4-byte Fp values)\n\n### 2. Frac Type (Extension Field Fraction)\n\n**File**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/include/frac_ext.cuh`\n\n**Type Definition (lines 6-9)**:\n```cuda\nstruct FracExt {\n    FpExt p;\n    FpExt q;\n};\n```\n\n**Key Facts**:\n- Represents a fraction in the extension field as numerator/denominator\n- `FracExt.p` is the numerator (FpExt)\n- `FracExt.q` is the denominator (FpExt)\n- Provides helper functions: `frac_add()`, `frac_unadd()`, `frac_add_inplace()`, `frac_unadd_inplace()`\n- Example usage in logup_round0.cu (line 292): `sums[c].p += eq * numer_results[c];` and `sums[c].q += eq * (denom_results[c] + denom_sum_init);`\n\n### 3. Existing .cu File Examples\n\n**File**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu`\n\n**Headers (lines 1-16)*