{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01JUaQLY5tCneACX1UGJv1uy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017884xdGXtsCBr6CwTCtkrt","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nGPU-side Round 0 polynomial extraction via pre-computed transform matrices\n\nReplace per-AIR D2H sync + CPU post-processing (transpose, iDFT, Lagrange\ninterpolation, coefficient adjustment) in the Round 0 multi-stream loop with\nGPU-side extraction kernels. Pre-compute transformation matrices on the CPU\nthat capture the entire pipeline as a matrix-vector multiply, upload once to\nGPU, then each AIR's extraction is a small <<<1, 64>>> kernel launch on the\nsame stream — no cudaStreamSynchronize between evaluation and the next AIR.\n\nKey changes:\n- New CUDA kernel file round0_extract.cu with zerocheck and logup extraction\n- Pre-computed Round0ExtractTables per unique constraint degree\n- Pre-allocated device batch array for all polynomial coefficients\n- Single D2H copy at end replaces ~1246 per-AIR pipeline drains\n- process_air_round0 now returns Result<()> instead of Round0AirResult\n\nRound 0 at APC 300: 245ms -> 202ms (1.21x). No regression at APC 0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"","description":"Commit the implementation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":169,"cache_read_input_tokens":155782,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":169},"output_tokens":55,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"48b5d5bc-06ba-4812-85f4-27a650fcd6d2","uuid":"c13622bf-8679-4474-bcc2-358561fb3ec7"}
